+## Document scaling defaults
+
+The Print dialog reads the current PDF's `/ViewerPreferences /PrintScaling` when it opens.
+`/None` initializes Size / Actual size; absent, `/AppDefault` and unrecognized values use the
+application's remembered manual handling and sizing. Automatic initialization is not remembered
+as a manual choice. Reopening the dialog reads the preset again; manual controls remain effective
+for the current print operation, including choices made before Cancel.
+
+`doc_print` with omitted or null optional `layout` selects actual for `/None`, otherwise fit,
+following the normal optional-argument semantics. An explicit layout string wins.
+The engine's fully resolved `print::Settings` are never rewritten by this preference. This covers
+the PDF 1.x default from ISO 32000-1 Table 150, not other print presets or PDF 2.0 Enforce.
+
